  "description": "Having lost her husband, Hae Jin-Ya marries Yeon U-Hui, her late husband's disciple. Dressed in black mourning clothes, Hae Jin-Ya gazed at Yeon U-Hui. In that moment, he extinguished the candles, reached out to her, and began to move his hips. Amidst the confusion, Jin-Ya found her body and mind gradually consumed by the pleasure U-Hui offered her. Over it all, the voice of a boy she had heard long ago overlapped.\n\n *“When I grow up, I'm going to marry you, Master.”*\n\nU-Hui, who had loved only Jin-Ya since childhood, and Jin-Ya, who felt guilty accepting this immoral love. Was their relationship, crossing the forbidden line, truly love? Or was it an irreversible fate?\n\n(Source: Ridibooks, translated)",
